    "updated_at": "2019-05-07T13:28:18Z",
    "body": "I found https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26183#c20 and also https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=5851. The general gist is that something might be feasible, but we don't want to add named string properties (which `iterable<Node>` would) as they'd clash with the named getters the object already has.",
