    "created_at": "2019-05-07T14:28:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-07T14:28:36Z",
    "body": "Wasn't aware of that, thanks. Is it not optimised because the spec makes that hard, or just because it hasn't been done yet? In the former case I'd agree that we should just let `getElementsByClassName` die, but in the latter, it feels like we should make the function more useful to motivate improving it.\r\n\r\nIt goes without saying - I'm very new to this so you're probably right, but I want to understand the decision as best as I can :)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
